{"type":"standard","title":"Troy Nehls","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Troy Nehls</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q96741441","titles":{"canonical":"Troy_Nehls","normalized":"Troy Nehls","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Troy Nehls</span></span>"},"pageid":64360777,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Troy_Nehls_117th_U.S_Congress.jpg/330px-Troy_Nehls_117th_U.S_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/34/Troy_Nehls_117th_U.S_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1536,"height":1920},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1378193029","tid":"794acf9a-bf20-11f1-a83b-8ff750b3c63d","timestamp":"2026-10-03T11:49:22Z","description":"American politician (born 1968)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troy_Nehls","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troy_Nehls?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troy_Nehls?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Troy_Nehls"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troy_Nehls","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Troy_Nehls","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troy_Nehls?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Troy_Nehls"}},"extract":"Troy Edwin Nehls is an American politician and former law-enforcement officer serving as the U.S. representative for Texas's 22nd congressional district since 2021. Before his election to Congress, he served as the sheriff for Fort Bend County, Texas from 2013 to 2021. Nehls is a member of the Republican Party.","extract_html":"<p><b>Troy Edwin Nehls</b> is an American politician and former law-enforcement officer serving as the U.S. representative for Texas's 22nd congressional district since 2021. Before his election to Congress, he served as the sheriff for Fort Bend County, Texas from 2013 to 2021. Nehls is a member of the Republican Party.</p>"}